157
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:07,020
The topic it covered was really interesting.

158
00:08:07,880 --> 00:08:08,100
Animal rights.

159
00:08:08,880 --> 00:08:09,920
Do you really believe in that?

160
00:08:10,600 --> 00:08:13,480
If they're going to focus on something, they should do it on civil rights.

161
00:08:14,060 --> 00:08:20,100
Yes, but we can't deny that animals are vulnerable, defenseless, and are completely at the mercy of human beings.

162
00:08:20,620 --> 00:08:24,440
I understand your point, but we continue to have transgressions against human rights.

163
00:08:25,040 --> 00:08:32,280
If so much attention weren't devoted to the topic of animals, we would then concentrate more on saving a human being instead of protecting a koala.

164
00:08:32,840 --> 00:08:34,640
You can't compare apples and oranges.

165
00:08:35,080 --> 00:08:38,100
I believe that both topics are important and that we can't ignore them.

166
00:08:38,460 --> 00:08:41,440
The mistreatment of animals can cause a great environmental imbalance.

167
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:45,760
I believe that governments should prohibit activities like poaching.

168
00:08:45,760 --> 00:08:47,520
Well, you are right on that point.

169
00:08:48,200 --> 00:08:51,520
This is the reason that I don't buy leather and I try to buy synthetic products.

170
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:53,380
At least you're doing your part.

171
00:08:54,040 --> 00:08:57,520
My contribution is to have a pet in the house that I treat like a member of the family.

172
00:08:57,960 --> 00:09:00,220
As long as you don't treat it better than your wife, it's fine.

173
00:09:01,440 --> 00:09:09,040
All right, so a debatable topic, animals and animal rights.

174
00:09:09,040 --> 00:09:09,380
What do you think?

175
00:09:10,040 --> 00:09:11,120
Well, I'll say this.

176
00:09:11,500 --> 00:09:17,120
I would be a hypocrite if I said that it's bad to hurt animals because I'm a meat eater.

177
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:19,640
I like to eat meat and I like to wear leather.

178
00:09:20,320 --> 00:09:22,920
But I do think it's bad to mistreat animals.

179
00:09:23,240 --> 00:09:39,880
So I try to buy free-range chicken or meat from places I know that treat the animals well and I definitely disagree with poaching and with using animals, especially endangered animals for money and cash purposes.

180
00:09:39,880 --> 00:09:41,520
And so that's my position.

181
00:09:41,520 --> 00:09:42,520
But what's yours?

182
00:09:42,520 --> 00:09:44,080
I mean, I know you eat meat too.

183
00:09:44,080 --> 00:09:45,360
No, yeah, of course.

184
00:09:45,360 --> 00:09:57,560
And I think even though protection of animals is a very important topic and you don't want the mistreatment of these little creatures that are very vulnerable to us because we're smarter than them in the end.

185
00:09:59,240 --> 00:10:05,710
But I think also it has to do a lot with superstition sometimes and kind of mystical and magical things.

186
00:10:06,760 --> 00:10:16,360
For example, people killing rhinos because they believe that the rhino horn has amazing curing properties or the same thing with elephant tusks and stuff like that.

187
00:10:16,360 --> 00:10:21,920
So it also involves this certain aspect that people almost don't know any better.

188
00:10:22,250 --> 00:10:25,510
They just truly believe that these things actually work or that they will help them.

189
00:10:25,760 --> 00:10:32,690
So they don't consider the, like in the dialogue said, the imbalance that they create in the environment or the consequences.

190
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:37,550
Or there might be some very serious evolutionary consequences that we cannot even imagine.

191
00:10:37,960 --> 00:10:43,200
And so, you know, things change kind of over time, sometimes quickly and sometimes slowly.

192
00:10:43,200 --> 00:10:47,640
But if we force change really quickly, who knows what the results are going to be.

193
00:10:47,640 --> 00:10:49,200
It might be really negative for us.

194
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:49,500
Exactly.

195
00:10:49,800 --> 00:10:50,920
And that's what we want to know now.

196
00:10:51,240 --> 00:10:53,760
What do you think about these topics?

197
00:10:53,760 --> 00:10:57,640
Because in the end, the environment, animals, they're all connected.

198
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:06,360
If you wipe out all the foxes in a forest, then you're going to have too many snakes running around, right?

199
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:07,260
So what do you think?

